Merging a library clones the expressions of its debug info, which can change
the size of their operations. Check that the relocation map follows each
address in them, through three levels of merging: libexpressions is merged
into libexpressions_mid, itself merged into libexpressions_top.

- In loclist.c, the location list of p holds DW_OP_addrx g1, then
  DW_OP_addrx g2. The operations keep indexing .debug_addr, whose entries
  carry the relocations.
- In hash.c, the location of secret computes an offset with DW_OP_convert
  operations, then adds the address of kSecret.

Instructions to reproduce
-------------------------

The clang is one built from this repository, as Xcode's does not emit such
location lists yet. Linking needs ld64, for -make_mergeable.

$ cd llvm/test/tools/dsymutil
$ I=Inputs/mergeable-libs
$ D=$I/dwarf5
$ CC="clang -target arm64-apple-macos15 -isysroot / -g -gdwarf-5 -O2 \
    -mllvm -accel-tables=Disable -fdebug-compilation-dir=/tmp \
    -fdebug-prefix-map=$(clang -print-resource-dir)=/clang"
$ LINK="xcrun clang -target arm64-apple-macos15 -dynamiclib \
    -Wl,-oso_prefix,$(pwd -P)/ -Wl,-segalign,0x1000"
$ for f in loclist hash expressions_mid expressions_top; do
    $CC -c $I/$f.c -o $D/$f.o
  done
$ ZERO_AR_DATE=1 $LINK -Wl,-make_mergeable \
    -install_name /path/to/libexpressions.dylib $D/loclist.o $D/hash.o \
    -o $D/libexpressions.dylib
$ ZERO_AR_DATE=1 $LINK -Wl,-make_mergeable \
    -install_name /path/to/libexpressions_mid.dylib $D/expressions_mid.o \
    -Wl,-merge_library,$D/libexpressions.dylib -o $D/libexpressions_mid.dylib
$ ZERO_AR_DATE=1 $LINK $D/expressions_top.o \
    -Wl,-merge_library,$D/libexpressions_mid.dylib -o $D/libexpressions_top.dylib

The accelerator tables are disabled as clang omits the base types of
DW_OP_convert from them, which fails the input verification of dsymutil.

DEFINE: %{l1} =
DEFINE: %{l2} =
DEFINE: %{l3} =
DEFINE: %{in} = %p/../Inputs/mergeable-libs/dwarf5
DEFINE: %{out} = %t/%{l1}-%{l2}-%{l3}
DEFINE: %{dsymutil} = dsymutil -oso-prepend-path=%p/..
DEFINE: %{link} = \
DEFINE:   mkdir -p %{out}/l1 %{out}/l2 \
DEFINE:   && %{dsymutil} --linker %{l1} %{in}/libexpressions.dylib \
DEFINE:        -o %{out}/l1/libexpressions.dylib.dSYM 2>&1 | count 0 \
DEFINE:   && %{dsymutil} --linker %{l2} -D %{out}/l1 \
DEFINE:        %{in}/libexpressions_mid.dylib \
DEFINE:        -o %{out}/l2/libexpressions_mid.dylib.dSYM 2>&1 | count 0 \
DEFINE:   && %{dsymutil} --linker %{l3} -D %{out}/l2 \
DEFINE:        %{in}/libexpressions_top.dylib \
DEFINE:        -o %{out}/libexpressions_top.dylib.dSYM 2>&1 | count 0 \
DEFINE:   && llvm-dwarfdump --debug-info --debug-addr \
DEFINE:        %{out}/libexpressions_top.dylib.dSYM | FileCheck %s

RUN: rm -rf %t
REDEFINE: %{l1} = classic
REDEFINE: %{l2} = classic
REDEFINE: %{l3} = classic
RUN: %{link}

The addresses are those of libexpressions_top.

CHECK:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/loclist.c")
CHECK:      DW_AT_location (0x{{[0-9a-f]+}}:
CHECK-NEXT:   [0x00000000000004a8, 0x00000000000004ac): DW_OP_addrx 0x4, DW_OP_stack_value
CHECK-NEXT:   [0x00000000000004ac, 0x00000000000004b4): DW_OP_addrx 0x5, DW_OP_stack_value)
CHECK-NEXT: DW_AT_name ("p")

CHECK:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/hash.c")
CHECK:      DW_AT_location ({{.*}}, DW_OP_convert {{.*}}, DW_OP_addr 0x56c, DW_OP_plus, DW_OP_stack_value)
CHECK-NEXT: DW_AT_abstract_origin ({{.*}} "secret")

The entries 4 and 5 of the address table of loclist.c are g1 and g2.

CHECK:      .debug_addr contents:
CHECK:      0x0000000000000484
CHECK-NEXT: 0x00000000000004a0
CHECK-NEXT: 0x00000000000004ac
CHECK-NEXT: 0x00000000000004b0
CHECK-NEXT: 0x000000000000100c
CHECK-NEXT: 0x0000000000001008
